// @@@ If the index is valid (between 0 and the size of the list), then for every index from 0 up to but not including the specified index, either both the current and old values at that index are null, or the current value at that index is equal to its old value.
--------------------
// @@@ If the index is valid (non-negative and less than the size of the list), then for every index from 0 up to but not including the specified index, each element at these indices remains unchanged or continues to be null if it was null before.
